{{DISPLAYTITLE: <span class="text-legendary";">Wizard Trio</span>}}
{{Protection}}{{MagicWords}}{{EventCard}}

{{Card Infobox|Cost=7|Rarity=Legendary|Type=Troop|ReleaseDate=27 May 2024}}
{{Quote|All three Wizards in one neat package.}}
The Wizard Trio was a temporary {{Rarity|Legendary}} [[Cards|card]] only available in certain Events. It spawned a [[Wizard]], an [[Ice Wizard]], and an [[Electro Wizard]] in a horizontal formation immediately after being deployed without any deploy time. The Wizard will spawn between the Ice Wizard from the left, and the Electro Wizard from the right. A Wizard Trio card costs 7 [[Elixir]] to deploy.

==Strategy==
*Like the individual Wizards, the Wizard Trio is very weak to medium [[:Category:Spell Cards|spells]], such as the [[Poison]] and [[Fireball]]. If both the spells hit all three Wizards, the damage will result in a large positive Elixir trade.
*The Wizard Trio has an incredibly high DPS, easily being able to decimate many tanks due to the Wizard, while heavily slowing them down and stunning them due to the Ice Wizard and Electro Wizard respectively. Additionally, the amount of splash damage from the Wizard and Ice Wizard can dispose off swarms, such as [[Bats/Evolution|Evolved Bats]], [[Rascals]], [[Elite Barbarians]], [[Goblin Gang]], [[Minion Horde]], [[Skeleton Army]], [[Zappies]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Royal Recruits/Evolution|Evolved Royal Recruits]], [[Three Musketeers]], [[Skeleton Dragons]], and [[Barbarians/Evolution|Evolved Barbarians]] with ease, and with the amount of stun from the Electro Wizard, they can take down troops such as [[Dark Prince]], [[Sparky]], [[Mighty Miner]], [[Prince]], [[Inferno Dragon]], [[Battle Ram/Evolution|Evolved Battle Ram]], and [[Bowler]].
*The [[Mega Knight]] is a very effective defensive counter to the Wizard Trio. His spawn damage is able to hit all 3 Wizards at once and with the help of the [[:Category:Crown Towers|Crown Tower]], he can easily destroy them, leaving the Mega Knight almost untouched for a counterattack.
*The [[Royal Delivery]], with the help of the [[Cannoneer]] or [[Dagger Duchess]] can fully counter the Wizard Trio for a large +4 positive Elixir trade. However, the [[Royal Recruits|Royal Recruit]] will get destroyed in the process, so there will be no counterattack.
*Since the Ice Wizard and the Electro Wizard deal spawn damage, deploying the Wizard Trio directly onto on small swarms and [[:Category:Building Cards|building]]-targeting tanks may be beneficial in certain situations, such as with [[Giant]], [[Lava Hound]], [[Golem]], or [[Skeleton Army]].

